WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.420
In the Japanese text

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.160
The hooded woman defers to the crow-like creature as "father"

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.280
But, she means it in a religious sense,

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.960
Not a paternal one

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.680
So it's more like the word "reverent"

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:34.520
"Godfather"

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.380
Or, perhaps, most accurately,

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.660
"Allfather"

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.940
And if you're invested in the lore of these games

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.640
Then you already know who this is.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.280
"Allfather Lloyd"

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.000
Lloyd was said to be the uncle to Lord Gwyn

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.200
And he was a focus of worship within the way of white

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.960
Which was this holy covenant devoted to the gods

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.560
And, to the maintenance of the bonfires

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.020
And in particular, Lloyd was known for his cleric knights

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.240
And he was praised for their undead hunts

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.200
Which were succesful partly because of Lloyd's Talismans

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.300
Which were these thrown items that block undead recovery via Estus

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.320
And in the earlier footage we saw Lloyd flaying himself

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.940
Over a lordvessel full of this liquid fire

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.120
Which is... Like Estus, really.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.920
So, this creature being Lloyd is a certainty, to me.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:34.460
Most notably, Lloyd is no longer a proud man like he's described previously.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.060
In fact, in the current age of Dark Souls III,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:42.500
Allfather Lloyd is described as being "long-forgotten" by the Way of White

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.900
And the clerics of Carim stand strong in their assertion

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:52.880
That Lloyd was always a derivative fraud with his "Allfather" title self-proclaimed.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.440
It makes sense then, that he should appear in the world

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.760
of The Forlorn,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.220
The Unwanted, and

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.180
The Exiled

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.500
The Painted World of Ariandelle

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.860
And Miyazaki has confirmed that the DLC takes place

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.220
in The Painted World

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.940
Albeit, a different 'Painted World'

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.020
There's this article from Polygon that I'm going to talk about,

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:17.180
Which mentions quite a few things that you wouldn't have caught if you just watched the trailer.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.960
So first, Miyazaki says that,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.820
He's aiming for a more "Gothic flavor," in

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:26.700
Not just this DLC, but the next DLC as well.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.360
They're... Linked in this sense, the two DLC's.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.760
They're said to be somewhat unique from the base game

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:38.720
And IGN-Japan reports that the focus is on the second DLC

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.600
To complete and finish the story.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.200
There will be two new bosses

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.920
And... We've actually seen all elements

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.840
Of both of the fights.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.960
In what is presumably the main boss fight,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.200
The female character clearly serves as phase 1,

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.300
Displaying this dominance over the tied-up Allfather.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.360
As to the woman's identity...

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.620
She's actually been mentioned in-game already.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.980
The Corvian Greatscythe reads,

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.680
"The Mistress of the Painted World is said to wield a great scythe, herself,"

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.160
And, we always assumed this was referring to

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.160
Priscilla, of Dark Souls 1

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.460
But, since the word "mistress" actually means,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.940
"A woman, in position of authority or control..."

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.620
It's clearly, in my opinion, referring to this woman,

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.920
Someone with a thematic connection to Priscilla,

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.780
With the Corvians, and

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.700
With the Way of White, also.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.040
Perhaps, this woman is Lloyd's apostle,

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.040
Mentioned in the White Seance Ring description?

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.160
Perhaps she's Gertrude,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.420
A woman described as a heretic,

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.580
Which might explain the source of the heretical stories

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.640
The winged Corvians tell all throughout the land.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:54.340
Or, perhaps, she's as yet unnamed.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.320
I read that there were a lot of people crying, "Velka!"

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.320
As soon as they saw her, and

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.780
Honestly, I'd be a bit dissapointed if this was Velka,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.000
I don't envision Velka this...

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.220
God that the other gods and lords fear,

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.540
I don't envision her as a simple humanoid being, to be honest.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.200
The other boss fight starts with a human duel as well,

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.380
With the wolf joining the fight after the defender falls,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.000
According to Polygon.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.920
But interestingly, in the trailer we don't see the wolf join the fight after the death of the human,

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:32.240
We see him join immediately after this shield bash.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.880
So, why is that?

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.900
Why is there a discrepancy in the information here?

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.060
My best guess is that the flash of the wolf's face here when you get shield bashed,

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.540
Might trigger the wolf's appearance in the fight early,

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.060
If you get caught by it.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.760
And, considering that this human enemy is so oddly dressed,

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.500
And actually a player-like NPC,

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.260
Do you think that this could be a sign that this is an actual player?

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.860
Like, in the mirror knight fight from Dark Souls II for example?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.740
I hope so, that was one of the best encounters in Dark Souls II.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.860
And, I love the way the wolf fights. I just have to say that.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.660
It's so reminiscent of Sif, and

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:17.260
I do believe it is Sif, or at least, it's an incarnation of him,

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.180
Just like Osiris was an incarnation of Seith, for example.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.820
The visual details are... Identical,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.280
His face and his eyes are exactly the same,

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:31.020
I can't wait to find out more about why he's here, and

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.300
I do really hope they fleshed out this part of the story, cause

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:38.840
They run the risk of this just being a shallow throwback if they don't flesh it out.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.800
Anyway, my favorite move of his is this one,

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.620
Where he misses you to kick up all the snow,

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.420
And then he attacks you from within the mist,

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:51.960
It's this fighting style that's consistent with how the wolves are described in-game

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:56.260
As enemies, how they confound their prey when they fight,

00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:00.640
And, regularly sized wolves are enemies in the DLC too

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.560
Though, we only see one in the trailer...

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.500
He's hidden, at the back, here.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.660
Polygon describes them as devious,

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.240
They say they watch from a distance and they maintain

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.800
that distance until the entire pack is gathered

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.620
and only then will they all attack at once.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:23.860
And, I like that. I think it's really important for the designers of this DLC

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:28.480
To keep the player's mind occupied with visual elements,

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.660
like the wolves constantly threatening you. That's a great one.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.660
Because, in open level design, like this,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:39.940
It's easy to get a bit bored because you don't quite need the same awareness you do when

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.600
You're traversing a complex dungeon and its traps.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:48.740
Other enemies include these 'Tree Women,' which I'm guessing are "Witch Trees."

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.480
As the Witchtree Stave item description says that,

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.740
"They're customary in the Far North."

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:59.020
And, we know that the North is a cold place from the Northern Set,

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.600
And there are enemies wearing very Northern-Set-Esque armor.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.940
Anyways, regardless of what they're called,

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.840
These long-limbed trees will grab at you if you come too close,

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:14.140
And they hurl orbs of flame at you if you stray too far.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:18.160
The other main enemies in this area are the Hollow Warriors

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.880
With the pointed helms.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.600
And at first I thought these might be members of Farron's Undead Legion,

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:28.560
As the pointed steel helm is described as a distinctive symbol of their's,

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.900
Plus, it makes some sense for them to be here because Sif is here as well,

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.080
And the Great Wolf and its blood is an object of their worship,

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.460
So if they are Warriors of Farron,

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.680
Perhaps that explains why the warrior with Sif

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:47.040
has a sorcerer's staff upon his or her hip,

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.820
Because Farron were known for the sorceries they develop as well.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:56.920
However, the sorcerer's staff is something given to sorcerers of the Vinheim Dragon School,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.060
And, looking a bit closer,

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:02.540
the pointed helms on the warriors actually look

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.260
visually a bit more like the Northern Helm,

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:09.580
Though, admittedly, they are taller and more narrow than that helm.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.900
Plus, many of these enemies use shields which the Undead Legion aren't known for.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.780
My second-best guess is that they're the cleric knights of Lloyd.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.980
Their straight swords have only a slight hint of a crossguard,

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.800
Just like the sword upon Lloyd's Sword Ring.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:30.980
Their shields have the same shape as the shields upon Lloyd's Shield Ring as well.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:35.760
And, their affinity with fire might make them related to Lloyd, who

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.880
We're certain is at the end of the DLC.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:40.340
But let's move on.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.500
Polygon states there will be four new spells.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.460
Four full new armor sets.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.800
And fifteen new weapons.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.340
The most interesting of which, to me, is this spear,

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:55.440
Which has a weapon art whereby you can throw the spear as a javelin,

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.900
and then magically have it reappear back in your hand...

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.760
Another interesting thing is the short Gladius-like sword,

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:05.960
and the shield that the wolf companion uses.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:10.340
This stance he or she is in, is totally unique,

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:15.460
And I wonder if it's a quality of the shield or the sword, or both.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.800
So, yeah, that pretty much wraps things up.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.820
Subscribe, for more Ashes content, and

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:27.420
Please comment below if you think that there's something I missed because I'd love to read it and so would others.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:32.720
We've usually got some really good discussions going on down there and I think our comment section is one of the best.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:37.060
And, in the spirit of trying to shout-out someone every video,

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:41.680
I'd love to direct you to a growing channel named, "The Ashen Hollow,"

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:47.200
Jake has been doing a great job breaking down some of the more specific questions of the series,

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:54.560
And, he has a particularly good couple of videos on Velka and his theories surrounding her.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.980
So, let's see if they get proven right or wrong in the coming months.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.000
Thanks for watching, again, and special thanks to Patrons.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.220
I'll see you next week.

